sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia--claude-opus-5-5--3> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Scutoid frequency vs curvature in segmented 3D epithelia against minimal energy" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia> ;
    dct:description "Biological part. For each 3D epithelial dataset (Gómez-Gálvez et al. 2018 salivary glands and egg chambers; PlantSeg Arabidopsis ovule and lateral-root volumes as a curved plant epithelium; other open segmented volumes on IDR and EMPIAR), compute per-cell apico-basal neighbour exchanges (scutoid indicator) and the local radial expansion ratio s = R_basal/R_apical from fitted tissue surfaces. Prediction: run a 3D Voronoi tube model (Gómez-Gálvez 2018) and a Surface Evolver relaxed-foam model on a tube or ellipsoid with the measured s, cell number and cell-size dispersion, giving the predicted scutoid fraction p̂(s) with simulation intervals. Pre-registered tolerance: supports energy minimization if observed scutoid fractions fall within the 95% simulation band at ≥ 80% of curvature bins pooled across datasets; refutes if observed fractions are outside the band in the same direction in ≥ 50% of bins. Also test the Gómez-Gálvez et al. 2022 biophysical principle linking connectivity to s." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Observed versus predicted scutoid fraction across curvature bins in at least three independent tissue types, with a pre-registered verdict on whether cells adopt minimal-energy packings for their curvature." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: Segmentation errors in apical or basal surfaces create spurious neighbour exchanges at rates comparable to predicted scutoid fractions (estimate the error rate on manually checked cells); then the test is measurement-limited." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/data-test" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Pre-register datasets' admission criteria (3D cell segmentation with apical and basal surfaces), binning of s and the tolerance. 2. Download and checksum datasets; compute scutoid indicators and s per cell. 3. Run the Voronoi and relaxed-foam simulations at measured parameters; build p̂(s) bands. 4. Compare and report the verdict per dataset and pooled." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): tractable" ;
    skos:note "Tool: 3d-segmentation" ;
    skos:note "Tool: cell-geometry" ;
    skos:note "Tool: surface-evolver" ;
    skos:note "Tool: data-test" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-04> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-11> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-08> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch09-16> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/scutoids> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/empiar/> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05376-1> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cels.2022.06.003> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.57613> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Kelvin's problem in epithelia" .

  <https://github.com/scutoids> dct:title "Scutoids code and data (Gómez-Gálvez et al.)" ;
    dct:description "Voronoi tube model code and segmented data from the 2018 study" .
  <https://idr.openmicroscopy.org/> dct:title "Image Data Resource" ;
    dct:description "Additional segmented 3D epithelial volumes" .
  <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/empiar/> dct:title "EMPIAR" ;
    dct:description "Volume EM datasets of epithelia" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05376-1> dct:title "Scutoids are a geometrical solution to three-dimensional packing of epithelia" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Gómez-Gálvez et al. 2018, Scutoids are a geometrical solution to three-dimensional packing of epithelia" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cels.2022.06.003> dct:title "A quantitative biophysical principle to explain the 3D cellular connectivity in curved epithelia" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Gómez-Gálvez et al. 2022, A quantitative biophysical principle to explain the 3D cellular connectivity in curved epithelia" .
  <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.57613> dct:title "Accurate and versatile 3D segmentation of plant tissues at cellular resolution" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Wolny et al. 2020, PlantSeg 3D segmentation of plant tissues" .
}

